Original commit body from 71932c662514a0fae21b958a71c9e1f60b254e3c:

Found when release-check's full suite and `ci-debug cron-status` were
read before preparing 9.0.0. Each was reproduced before it was fixed.

1. owner_ancestry.py re-declared the member-name separator tuple, which
   test_member_names' live-tree linter forbids (test-all-packages and
   all four nightly legs). It now imports MEMBER_NAME_SEPARATORS.

2. catalog.build_catalog_from_registries recorded each linker through
   the analyzer loop's variable (`seen.add(reg.name)`), a leftover of
   7a6b18b5ee's rename. With analyzers registered it recorded the last
   analyzer's name; with none (hypergumbo-core installed alone) it raised
   UnboundLocalError, which killed measure-taint-precision.py on a
   core-only tree. New test: a linkers-only registry builds a catalog
   listing exactly those linkers (red before, green after). Unreleased.

   TestINVHujogClosureCriterion built the catalog before anything
   imported cli, so run alone (smart-test on test_catalog.py, on dev
   too) it saw no linkers; an autouse fixture now imports cli first.

3. The cron test-agent-infra step installed no pytest-cov, and
   smart-test always passes --cov, so pytest exited 4 (usage error)
   before collecting and all five test_smart_test_zero_collect tests
   failed there. Reproduced in a venv with exactly that step's packages
   (5 failed), green with pytest-cov added; tests/ then passes in full in
   that venv (2211 passed). The INV-tazur behaviour was right; its tests
   had never run in CI. The dormant GitHub copy gets the same line.

4. measure_code_tree.pin accepted HG_MEASURE_TREE=pythonpath when
   PYTHONPATH supplied core but not the language packages and those
   resolved nowhere else: announce() then saw one tree. It now refuses
   from PYTHONPATH alone, so the verdict does not depend on what else is
   installed.

Tests: smart-test 25394 passed, changed sources at 100%; root tests for
the scripts 40 passed in the dev venv.

Not in this commit: the test-only-reachability and self-claims gates,
also red on the cron; they follow separately.

